        <Summary>Userspace virtual machine and processor emulator</Summary>
        <Description>QEMU is a generic and open source machine emulator and virtualizer. It emulates a full system (for example a PC), including a processor and various peripherals, and can be used to launch different operating systems without rebooting the PC or to debug system code. In user-mode emulation mode, QEMU can launch Linux processes compiled for one CPU on another CPU.</Description>
